{
  "kata": "facade",
  "candidate_law": "facade trace law: a facade entry point fronts several subsystem actions, and the implementation realizes the documented composition - every documented call has an implementation under the same entry point performing the same subsystem action (completeness), every implemented call belongs to a documented call with the same action (attribution), an entry point makes a given subsystem call at most once (multiplicity), and each call observes its subsystem action's outcome (transparency).",
  "residual_gaps": "three facade-defining clauses have no predicate on the kernel surface: (1) the entry point's aggregate outcome is a fold over the fiber of call_facade - equations compose forward only, the aggregate is a forward leaf, and there is no fold, identity, or reverse composition; (2) call order is not representable - Call rows are an unordered set and dense ids are name-sorted presentation; (3) surface reduction/coverage - there is no cardinality or existential predicate, so 'the facade exposes no more operations than the subsystem' and 'every promised capability is covered' are unstatable. A fourth, model-side gap: spec aliasing (two documented calls naming one implemented call) is not observable without an identity arrow.",
  "comparison_rule": "an element is call:<FacadeOp>/<Action> or op:<FacadeOp>. The baseline identifies an element only when one of its frozen conventional assertions fails on it: composition (the sampled entry point's call-pair multiset equals the documented one), aggregate (the entry point's outcome equals the documented aggregate), and per-call transparency (a sampled pair's call outcome equals the named action's outcome). The probe identifies an element only when a check finding's witness resolves to it: an equation witness resolves by its source object's row pair, a key witness by the colliding rows' pair, a dangling witness by the source row's pair. unique = executed probe elements minus baseline-identified elements. Hypothesized underconstraint findings are discovery questions recorded verbatim, never counted as detections.",
  "hypotheses_expected": [
    "parallel_paths:call_action∘action_outcome=call_facade∘facade_outcome",
    "parallel_paths:call_facade∘facade_outcome=call_outcome",
    "parallel_paths:spec_action∘action_outcome=spec_facade∘facade_outcome",
    "parallel_paths:spec_action∘action_outcome=spec_impl∘call_outcome",
    "parallel_paths:spec_facade∘facade_outcome=spec_impl∘call_outcome"
  ],
  "expressibility": {
